      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"CIP\", \"table_name\": \"CIP\", \"count\": 6, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_1618\", \"name\": \"School CIP Categories with Yearly Math IAP Max Enrollment Stddev and Department Phone\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school's name, the school's name in the commencement book, the maximum CIP program code among its degree-granting departments' courses (excluding the Mathematics department), the CIP category ('HIGH_CIP', 'LOW_CIP', or 'MEDIUM_CIP'), the academic year, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered by the Mathematics department in that year (considering only years with more than five activities), and the Mathematics department phone number, for schools where the maximum CIP program code is greater than 130000 and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of maximum enrollment is available? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3042\", \"name\": \"Engineering CIP Category Latest Start Term, Highest Version, and Most Active Department\", \"category\": \"CIP Program Classification and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each program category in the School of Engineering with a program version after 2000, what is the latest course start term, the highest program version, and the department that offers the most courses in that category, along with the count of courses from that department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3901\", \"name\": \"2012SU Subject Offerings Dense Rank Matched with Department-6 CIP Course Classification and School Rollups\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and CIP Program Classification Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2272\", \"name\": \"Math Department Unit Statistics with Course Level Student Counts and Lecture-Lab Unit Averages\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2365\", \"name\": \"Top 3 Most Offered Math Courses per Term with Description Counts, Min CIP Code, and Department Phone\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 3 most frequently offered courses in the Mathematics department, for each course and each term it was offered, display the course number, course description, subject title, number of times offered, department name, number of unique course descriptions for that course and department, the minimum CIP program code for that course and department, the term code, the term description, the school name, and the department phone number. Do not repeat the course number if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by course number and term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1033\", \"name\": \"Math Graduate Students School Dense Ranks Unioned with Department CIP Code Range-Variance\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department name, department full name, student full name, student email address, dense rank over the school code, CIP program code range, and CIP program code variance for all graduate students in degree-granting Mathematics departments, as well as for all Mathematics departments that are degree granting and have at least one course with a non-null CIP program code, including the CIP program code range and variance for those departments even if they have no such students. List the results ordered by department full name and student full name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
